  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You always have @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplCharmPerso]{Charm Person} and @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplMirrorImag]{Mirror Image} prepared.</p><p>In addition, immediately after you cast an Enchantment or Illusion spell with a spell slot, you can make a creature you can see within 60 feet of you make a Wisdom saving throw against your spell save DC. On a failure, it has the Charmed or Frightened condition (your choice) for 1 minute, repeating the save at the end of each of its turns and ending the effect on a success. Once you use this benefit, you can't use it again until you finish a Long Rest, but you can restore it by expending one use of your Bardic Inspiration (no action required).</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-9nCMHwB76iKxQshi\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>The effect is Charmed: swap it for Frightened if you choose that.</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
